# Service Layer Patterns and Guidelines

## Service Categories

### Background Services
- [background_service.dart](mdc:lib/services/background_service.dart) - Singleton service for heavy initialization tasks
  - Manages Google Sheets, API endpoints, and message checking
  - Provides network connectivity checking
  - Handles app initialization without blocking UI

### API Services
- [api_endpoint.dart](mdc:lib/services/api_endpoint.dart) - HTTP API communication
  - Handles endpoint binding and message checking
  - Implements network timeouts and error handling
  - Optimized message processing with Set operations

### Data Services
- [api_data_fetch.dart](mdc:lib/services/api_data_fetch.dart) - Google Docs content fetching
- [gsheet_access.dart](mdc:lib/services/gsheet_access.dart) - Google Sheets integration
  - Handles spreadsheet operations and data insertion
  - Implements proper timeout and error handling

## Service Design Patterns

### 1. Singleton Pattern
```dart
class MyService {
  static final MyService _instance = MyService._internal();
  factory MyService() => _instance;
  MyService._internal();
  
  // Service implementation
}
```

### 2. Network Timeout Implementation
```dart
Future<Response> fetchData() async {
  try {
    final response = await http.get(url)
        .timeout(Duration(seconds: 30));
    return response;
  } catch (e) {
    log('❌ Network error: $e');
    rethrow;
  }
}
```

### 3. Background Initialization
```dart
Future<void> initializeInBackground() async {
  if (_isLoading || _isInitialized) return;
  
  _isLoading = true;
  try {
    final futures = <Future>[];
    futures.add(_initializeService1());
    futures.add(_initializeService2());
    
    await Future.wait(futures, eagerError: false);
    _isInitialized = true;
  } finally {
    _isLoading = false;
  }
}
```

## Error Handling Standards

### 1. Logging
- Use `dart:developer` log function
- Include emoji prefixes for log levels: ✅ 🔄 ❌ ⚠️
- Log both success and failure scenarios

### 2. Exception Management
- Always wrap network calls in try-catch blocks
- Provide meaningful error messages to users
- Don't let services crash the app

### 3. Graceful Degradation
- Continue app functionality even if services fail
- Provide offline fallback where possible
- Cache data locally when appropriate

## Performance Optimization

### 1. Parallel Operations
- Use `Future.wait()` for independent operations
- Avoid sequential API calls when possible
- Implement proper concurrency management

### 2. Efficient Data Structures
- Use `Set` for O(1) lookups instead of `List.contains()`
- Use `Map` for key-value relationships
- Minimize data transformation overhead

### 3. Memory Management
- Dispose of resources properly
- Avoid memory leaks in singletons
- Use weak references where appropriate

## Integration with UI

### 1. Non-blocking Operations
- Never block the UI thread with heavy operations
- Use background services for initialization
- Provide loading states to users

### 2. State Synchronization
- Use callbacks or streams for UI updates
- Implement proper state management
- Handle race conditions

### 3. Network Connectivity
- Check connectivity before operations
- Handle offline scenarios gracefully
- Provide user feedback for network issues

## Testing Considerations
- Mock external dependencies
- Test timeout scenarios
- Verify error handling paths
- Test concurrent operations
